NOTE ON SCOPE

This MIT license covers the *code* in this repository only. The datasets are
licensed separately, as follows.

OURS. The human user-study data is our own work and we assert copyright over
it. This covers every participant response (answers, confidence ratings,
timings, concept clicks, answer changes, tab-switching), our models' outputs,
the experimental design, and -- for the CUB study -- the six concept
definitions and their ground-truth annotation, which we wrote and annotated
ourselves rather than taking from CUB. Released under CC-BY-4.0:

  - NWeak/CBM-user-study-cub      CC-BY-4.0, (c) 2026 the authors
  - NWeak/CBM-user-study-emails   CC-BY-4.0, (c) 2026 the authors
  - NWeak/emails-user-study       CC-BY-4.0, (c) 2026 the authors

NOT OURS. We do not own the underlying corpora and cannot relicense them:

  - NWeak/cub-mirror              CUB-200-2011 images and the official class
                                  and concept annotations, under Caltech's
                                  non-commercial research-use terms
                                  (Wah et al. 2011).
  - NWeak/emails-mirror           Derived from the PhishingSpamDataSet of
                                  Toth, Bisztray and Dubniczky
                                  (arXiv:2511.21448), CC-BY-4.0, attribution
                                  required.

WHERE THEY MEET. Two details sit inside our datasets but originate upstream:

  - CBM-user-study-cub's CorrectAnswer is the CUB species label for the
    stimulus, and StimID/TestSampleIdx reference CUB images (the images
    themselves are not included). Its FeatureN_GT columns are ours.
  - CBM-user-study-emails' and emails-user-study's FeatureN_GT / cN_gt columns
    are our six-concept merge of Toth et al.'s emotion and motivation
    annotations, so their attribution requirement reaches these columns.
    Everything else in those datasets is ours.

See each dataset card on the HuggingFace Hub, and the Acknowledgments section
of README.md, for the full attribution requirements.
